{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Base the increment on the existing Spring XD 1.x codebase (Java 8, Gradle build, Spring Boot 1.1.x); the Spring Boot version will be bumped to 1.1.7 to obtain backported SSL support required by U8, per the specification note.",
    "U1 JDBC source: implement as a standard XD source module using the Spring Integration JDBC inbound channel adapter with a poller; support full-table and incremental polling (timestamp/auto-increment column), externalized module options (url, driver, username, password, query, update mode, cron/fixed delay), and JDBC drivers supplied via module classpath rather than core distribution.",
    "U2 Redis sink: implement as an XD sink module backed by Spring Data Redis / Spring Integration Redis outbound adapter; default target is a Redis LIST (RPUSH) with configurable key, topic/structure, and serializer (String/JSON); connection configured via RedisConnectionFactory options (host, port, password).",
    "U6 Kafka sink: implement as an XD sink module using the Spring Integration Kafka outbound adapter with an async producer and batching to satisfy the 'mass data' requirement; module options for broker list, topic, partition key, and encoder/serializer.",
    "U3 ZK security: scope limited to ZooKeeper digest authentication plus zNode ACLs enforced through the Curator/ZK client ACL provider used by XD admin and container nodes; credentials and ACL scheme configurable in servers.yml; Kerberos/SASL explicitly out of scope for this increment.",
    "U4 Trigger SPI: define a public, documented Trigger interface (start/stop lifecycle + TriggerAction callback) and a module-level registration mechanism so custom triggers can be packaged inside XD modules; keep existing cron and fixed-delay triggers backward compatible by adapting them to the SPI.",
    "U5 custom module guidance: per the 11/20 scope update, deliver a working example custom module (Maven project) plus a developer guide; no archetype tooling changes in this increment.",
    "U7 e2e fix: fix the Grunt build/test orchestration (server lifecycle and keep-alive socket handling in the connect/protractor tasks) so server and protractor tests can run in a single process; no product code changes expected.",
    "U8 HTTPS: enable SSL via Spring Boot server.ssl.* properties (keystore path, password, key alias) exposed through XD admin configuration; ship a self-signed certificate generation recipe for development; both REST endpoints and Admin UI served over the secured connector.",
    "All new modules follow XD module packaging conventions, include unit tests, integration tests against embedded/local middleware, and asciidoc/wiki documentation."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "A single developer (the author) performs all work; estimates are person-days of effort, not elapsed time, and assume focused work on one activity at a time.",
    "The existing Spring XD codebase, Gradle build, and CI infrastructure are available and functional at the start of the increment.",
    "Integration test middleware (H2/MySQL/PostgreSQL, Redis, Kafka, and a multi-node ZooKeeper ensemble) is available locally or via containers/embedded servers without procurement effort.",
    "Spring Boot 1.1.7 (SNAPSHOT or release) artifacts are accessible from the configured Maven repositories.",
    "ZooKeeper security scope is digest authentication with ACLs; no Kerberos/SASL infrastructure is required.",
    "U7 is confined to build/test tooling configuration; no changes to application runtime code are needed.",
    "Documentation targets the project wiki/asciidoc and requires no separate publishing infrastructure.",
    "Estimates cover design, implementation, unit/integration testing, documentation, code review, and reasonable rework; they exclude organizational meetings, training, and release-management overhead beyond CI updates.",
    "Effort is estimated in ideal workdays of 8 hours."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "Design JDBC source module (U1)",
      "activity_description": "Define module options, polling semantics (full vs incremental), state handling for incremental queries, and error/restart behavior for the native JDBC source.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "Implement JDBC source module (U1)",
      "activity_description": "Implement the XD JDBC source module on top of the Spring Integration JDBC inbound adapter, including module configuration metadata and driver classpath handling.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "Unit tests for JDBC source (U1)",
      "activity_description": "Write unit tests for query building, incremental update logic, and option validation using an embedded database.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "Integration tests for JDBC source across databases (U1)",
      "activity_description": "Set up and run integration tests against representative databases (H2, MySQL, PostgreSQL) validating ingestion into XD streams.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "Document JDBC source module (U1)",
      "activity_description": "Write module reference documentation and stream definition examples for the JDBC source.",
      "most_likely_effort": 0.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "Design Redis sink module (U2)",
      "activity_description": "Define sink options: target structure (LIST default), key/topic, serializer, and Redis connection settings.",
      "most_likely_effort": 0.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "Implement Redis sink module (U2)",
      "activity_description": "Implement the XD Redis sink using Spring Data Redis / Spring Integration Redis outbound adapter with configurable serialization.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "Unit and integration tests for Redis sink (U2)",
      "activity_description": "Test the sink against embedded/local Redis covering payload encoding, key routing, and error paths.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A9",
      "activity_name": "Document Redis sink module (U2)",
      "activity_description": "Write reference documentation and usage examples for the Redis sink.",
      "most_likely_effort": 0.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A10",
      "activity_name": "Design ZooKeeper security model (U3)",
      "activity_description": "Define the authentication scheme (digest), zNode ACL layout for XD paths, and configuration surface in servers.yml for admin and container nodes.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A11",
      "activity_name": "Implement ZK authentication and ACL support (U3)",
      "activity_description": "Wire digest credentials and an ACL provider into the Curator/ZooKeeper client setup used by XD admin and containers; handle unauthenticated fallback and error reporting.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A12",
      "activity_name": "Integration testing on secured ZK ensemble (U3)",
      "activity_description": "Stand up a secured multi-node ZooKeeper ensemble and verify XD startup, stream deployment, and access restrictions for unauthorized clients.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A13",
      "activity_name": "Ops documentation and scripts for ZK security (U3)",
      "activity_description": "Document how to provision ACLs/credentials, configure XD nodes, and troubleshoot; provide helper scripts or commands.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A14",
      "activity_name": "Design Trigger extension SPI (U4)",
      "activity_description": "Specify the public Trigger interface, lifecycle contract, and module-level registration mechanism for custom triggers.",
      "most_likely_effort": 0.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A15",
      "activity_name": "Implement Trigger SPI and refactor existing triggers (U4)",
      "activity_description": "Implement the SPI, adapt built-in cron/fixed-delay triggers onto it, and keep existing stream definitions backward compatible.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A16",
      "activity_name": "Sample custom trigger and tests (U4)",
      "activity_description": "Build a sample custom trigger module plus unit/integration tests demonstrating the extension point.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A17",
      "activity_name": "Document Trigger SPI (U4)",
      "activity_description": "Document the SPI contract, packaging, and a walkthrough for implementing a custom trigger.",
      "most_likely_effort": 0.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A18",
      "activity_name": "Build example custom module project (U5)",
      "activity_description": "Create a working example custom module (source/processor/sink) demonstrating the recommended development approach, per the scoped-down requirement.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A19",
      "activity_name": "Write custom module developer guide (U5)",
      "activity_description": "Write the step-by-step guide covering project layout, module metadata, testing, packaging, and deployment of custom modules.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A20",
      "activity_name": "Review and publish custom module guidance (U5)",
      "activity_description": "Review the example and guide for accuracy against the codebase and publish to the project documentation/wiki.",
      "most_likely_effort": 0.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A21",
      "activity_name": "Design Kafka sink module (U6)",
      "activity_description": "Define producer options (brokers, topic, partition key, encoder/serializer, batching) suitable for high-volume publishing.",
      "most_likely_effort": 0.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A22",
      "activity_name": "Implement Kafka sink module (U6)",
      "activity_description": "Implement the XD Kafka sink using the Spring Integration Kafka outbound adapter with an asynchronous, batched producer.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A23",
      "activity_name": "Integration tests for Kafka sink (U6)",
      "activity_description": "Test publishing to an embedded/local Kafka broker, including partitioning, serialization, and throughput sanity checks.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A24",
      "activity_name": "Document Kafka sink module (U6)",
      "activity_description": "Write reference documentation and stream examples for the Kafka sink.",
      "most_likely_effort": 0.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A25",
      "activity_name": "Reproduce and root-cause e2e socket hang up (U7)",
      "activity_description": "Reproduce the 'Fatal error: socket hang up' with grunt test:e2e and diagnose the interaction between the served app and protractor in a single process.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A26",
      "activity_name": "Fix Grunt test orchestration (U7)",
      "activity_description": "Fix the Grunt configuration (server lifecycle, keep-alive/connection handling, task sequencing) so tests and server run reliably in one process.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A27",
      "activity_name": "Verify single-process e2e suite (U7)",
      "activity_description": "Run grunt test:e2e repeatedly to confirm the suite passes in one process without socket hang ups and without regressions.",
      "most_likely_effort": 0.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A28",
      "activity_name": "Update build to Spring Boot 1.1.7 (U8)",
      "activity_description": "Work through the Gradle build changes to pick up Spring Boot 1.1.7 and align dependent versions, resolving repository/snapshot resolution issues.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A29",
      "activity_name": "Implement HTTPS for Admin server (U8)",
      "activity_description": "Enable SSL on the XD Admin server via Spring Boot server.ssl.* properties, including keystore configuration and secure connector setup.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A30",
      "activity_name": "Test secured Admin endpoints and UI (U8)",
      "activity_description": "Verify REST API endpoints and the Admin UI over HTTPS, certificate handling, and that HTTP is disabled or redirected as configured.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A31",
      "activity_name": "Document HTTPS setup (U8)",
      "activity_description": "Document keystore generation (incl. self-signed dev recipe) and the configuration properties to enable HTTPS.",
      "most_likely_effort": 0.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A32",
      "activity_name": "Cross-module end-to-end stream testing",
      "activity_description": "Run end-to-end streams combining the new modules (e.g., JDBC source to Redis/Kafka sinks) on a secured deployment to validate the increment as a whole.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A33",
      "activity_name": "Regression suite execution and CI updates",
      "activity_description": "Update CI jobs for new tests/modules and run the full regression suite, fixing any fallout from the Spring Boot bump and new modules.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A34",
      "activity_name": "Code review and rework",
      "activity_description": "Incorporate peer review feedback across all stories, including refactoring, javadoc/checkstyle compliance, and test adjustments.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 40.5
  }
}

